## Summary
The article explores the declining trend of Americans, especially children, not reading entire books, particularly literary fiction. It qualifies the common narrative that 'the kids can’t read' by specifying that the issue is more about the type and extent of reading rather than illiteracy.

## Key Points
- The statement that 'the kids can’t read' is oversimplified and requires qualification.
- The problem is specific to Americans and focuses on not reading full books, especially literary fiction.
- The decline in reading affects not just children but also adults.
- Recent articles have brought attention to this phenomenon in American society.


